    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bd465469_0f98b5b8",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 198,
      "author": {
        "id": 1149894
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-09-18T20:16:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I arbitrarily picked 3. During testing, I\u0027ve not seen more than 1 message queued. But to test the queue, I sent 3 consecutive messages and verified that they were queued and sent later. Do you have a suggestion about the queue size?",
      "parentUuid": "900fa829_efa7eb12",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 198,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 198,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "068f479420203eb05b65458cd90ba92cd742221a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1211c2ba_70a69eb6",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 201,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000016
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-09-18T09:28:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would be slightly inclined to re-use queue.h rather than adding and debugging another variant.\nThe RAM overhead should be minimal.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 200,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 201,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "068f479420203eb05b65458cd90ba92cd742221a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7284b6f8_afc34a57",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 201,
      "author": {
        "id": 1149894
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-09-18T20:16:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I initially tried to use queue.h but it used more RAM. QUEUE_NULL(SIZE, TYPE) uses SIZE*sizeof(TYPE) units of data for the queue buffer. And to access that data, I needed to allocate an another buffer of length SIZE*sizeof(TYPE) to use queue_remove_units(struct queue const *q, void *dest, size_t count);",
      "parentUuid": "1211c2ba_70a69eb6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 200,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 201,
        "endChar": 16
      },
